Why Is Demand Increasing
Addressing Tumor Heterogeneity: Dual-antibody ADCs can recognize two targets or epitopes, creating opportunities to improve tumor coverage and address heterogeneous antigen expression.
Advances in ADC Engineering: Progress in antibody engineering, linker chemistry, site-specific conjugation, and payload selection is expanding the potential of next-generation ADC platforms.
Growing Oncology Development: Increasing clinical development activity across solid and non-solid tumors is creating new opportunities for dual-target and dual-epitope ADC technologies.

Dual-Antibody ADC Market Watch: Next-Generation Payload and Target Design
The market is increasingly focused on clinically validated target pairs, improved internalization, topoisomerase-I payloads, site-specific conjugation, and linker designs intended to improve therapeutic windows. Development activity is also expanding across dual-target and biparatopic constructs.

