Why This Market Matters
Dual-antibody ADCs represent an emerging area of oncology drug development combining multispecific antibody recognition with cytotoxic payload delivery. The approach is being explored to address tumor heterogeneity, resistance mechanisms, and target co-expression. Development increasingly depends on target-pair selection, payload performance, conjugation consistency, manufacturing scalability, and the ability to demonstrate an appropriate therapeutic window.

